I. FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS
1. Student Management Requirements
1.1. User Login:
- The system shall allow students to log in using their student ID and password.
- The system shall verify the student's login information before granting access.
- The system shall display an error message when the student enters an incorrect student ID or password.
1.2. User Logout:
- The system shall allow students to securely log out of their accounts.
- The system shall terminate the current login session after logout.
2. Course Management Requirements 
2.1. View Course List:
- The system shall display a list of available courses.
- The system shall show course ID, course name, number of credits, schedule, and available seats.
- The system shall allow students to view course information before registration.
2.2. Search Courses:
- The system shall allow students to search for courses by course ID or course name.
- The system shall display courses matching the search keywords.
- The system shall notify students when no matching courses are found.
2.3. View Course Details:
- The system shall display detailed information about a selected course.
- The system shall show the course schedule, number of credits, and maximum enrollment capacity.
3. Course Registration Requirements
3.1. Register for Courses:
- The system shall allow students to select and register for available courses.
- The system shall verify that the selected course exists.
- The system shall check whether the student has already registered for the selected course.
- The system shall check whether the course still has available seats.
- The system shall check for schedule conflicts with other registered courses.
- The system shall ensure that the total registered credits do not exceed 20 credits.
- The system shall save registration information when all conditions are satisfied.
- The system shall notify students whether registration is successful or unsuccessful.
3.2. Cancel Course Registration:
- The system shall allow students to cancel courses they have already registered for.
- The system shall verify the student's registration information before cancellation.
- The system shall update the available course seats after successful cancellation.
- The system shall notify students of the cancellation result.
3.3. View Registered Courses:
- The system shall allow students to view their registered courses.
- The system shall display course ID, course name, credits, and course schedule.
- The system shall calculate and display the total number of registered credits.
4. Registration Management Requirements 
4.1. Registration Validation:
- The system shall prevent students from registering for the same course more than once.
- The system shall prevent registration when the course has reached its maximum capacity.
- The system shall prevent students from registering for courses with overlapping schedules.
- The system shall prevent students from exceeding the maximum credit limit of 20 credits.
4.2. Update Registration Information:
- The system shall automatically update registration records after successful registration or cancellation.
- The system shall update the number of available seats after each registration transaction.
- The system shall ensure that registration information is stored accurately in the database.
5. Tuition Fee Payment Requirements
5.1. Calculate Tuition Fees
- The system shall automatically calculate tuition fees based on the total number of credits of courses registered by each student.
- The system shall display the price per credit.
- The system shall display the total tuition fee that each student needs to pay.
- The system shall update the tuition fee when a student adds or cancels a course.
5.2. View Payment Information
- The system shall allow students to view their tuition fee information.
- The system shall display student ID, total registered credits, total tuition fees, and payment status.
- The system shall display the tuition fee payment deadline.
5.3. Make Payment
- The system shall allow students to pay their tuition fees.
- The system shall support payment methods accepted by the university.
- The system shall confirm the transaction after successful payment.
- The system shall notify students when a payment fails.
- The system shall prevent duplicate payment transactions for the same tuition fee.
5.4. Payment History
- The system shall store students' payment history.
- The system shall display the payment amount, transaction date, and payment status for each transaction.
- The system shall allow students to review their previous payment transactions.
5.5. Payment Status Management
- The system shall automatically update payment status after each transaction.
- The system shall distinguish between the following payment statuses:
  - Unpaid.
  - Paid.
  - Payment Failed.
- The system shall store transaction information for verification and reconciliation purposes.
6. Course Administration Requirements
6.1. Manage Course Information
- The system shall allow authorized administrators to add new courses.
- The system shall allow administrators to update course information.
- The system shall allow administrators to delete courses.
- The system shall allow administrators to manage course capacity.
6.2. Manage Student Information
- The system shall allow authorized administrators to add student information.
- The system shall allow administrators to update student information.
- The system shall allow administrators to search for student accounts.
- The system shall allow administrators to manage student accounts.
6.3. View Registration Reports
- The system shall allow administrators to view course registration records.
- The system shall display the list of students registered for each course.
- The system shall provide course registration information for management purposes.
